      <activity id="f1454ecc-c2dc-582d-93aa-1b12adde1031" activityNameId="f685bb68-b51a-5d02-9ae2-10ae7bc68ca3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, natural/varnished, wall opening, to final disposal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, natural/varnished, wall opening, to final disposal
The amount of materials to be disposed of at the end of life was estimated based on the bill of materials. A cut-off approach is used for recycling of metals (aluminium and zinc). The functional unit is 1m2 of wall opening.;
UUID: 19c3a42e-f73a-4f83-a722-ce42fae00519
Included processes are the disposal of wood, glue, steel, plastics, paint, rubber. The transport to the municipal incineration plant is included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_19c3a42e-f73a-4f83-a722-ce42fae00519.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
